# 075 · Model usage for each run, campaign and the whole system

**Status:** `VERIFIED` · **Version:** [v0.1.0](../roadmap.md#v010) · **Part:** Running campaigns

## What

Every model call the agents make is counted, and control shows the totals:

- **Per call** (code records it, never an agent): the agent kind (workers, planner, teachers, auditor, review panel), the harness, the provider and the model; tokens in, split into cached and not cached where the provider says; tokens out (and reasoning tokens where the provider says); the time to the first token and the whole call's time, so output tokens a second.
- **A run's Overview:** the totals and the speed (tokens out a second, median and spread), for each agent kind and model.
- **A campaign's page:** the same, summed over all its runs, with each run's share.
- **The whole system** (Overview): the same over every campaign and rig, for a period (today, 7 days, all).
- **REST and MCP:** the same numbers, so they can be read without the dashboard.
- Where a harness does not report a figure (for example cached tokens), the screen says "not reported", never 0.

## Why

The owner, 2026-10-21: "overview on a capmaign run doesn't show total tokens used etc... Would love some model stats (tok/s, total tokens in / out / cache / not-cached, etc...)... And a roll up to campaign for all runs under it, and a roll up to entire system."

## Done when

- [x] The harness and the supervisor record each model call's usage and time, for every harness (Pi, OpenCode, Codex, Claude Code), as far as each reports it; the rig sends it to control with its events.
- [x] Control sums it per run, per campaign and for the system; REST and MCP give the sums.
- [x] The run's Overview, the campaign's page and the system Overview show them, after a mockup the owner approved.
- [x] Tests for the records, the sums and the "not reported" case; pages updated.
- [x] Cost: each call's cost from its model's price (the provider's list, or the owner's price in Settings › Providers), "on a plan" for subscriptions, "no price" where none is known, and a RunPod rig's pod spend, summed for a run, a campaign and the system, on the same screens and over REST and MCP.

## Decisions

- 2026-10-21, owner, on the mockup (`v010-usage`): "top of run page, side bar of campaign page, stats page for top level across the system (metrics tab)." So: a run's model use at the top of its page; a campaign's in its page's sidebar; the system's on a new **Metrics** page in the main navigation. The mockup's other choices are built as shown: no cost column, the median time to the first token, and "today" in the viewer's own time zone.
- 2026-10-21, owner: "Probably also want \"cost\" associated with stuff." So cost joins the model use (this replaces "no cost column" above): each call's cost is its tokens times its model's price (in, cached in, out), the price taken from the provider's model list when it gives one, else set by the owner in Settings › Providers; a subscription's calls show "on a plan" with their tokens; a model with no price shows "no price", never 0. A rig on RunPod adds its pod's spend, which control already tracks, to its runs' and campaigns' cost. Shown where the model use is: the run page's top, the campaign's sidebar and the Metrics page; REST and MCP give it too.
- 2026-10-21, build (the lead's brief left it open): each record is one `model_call` event of its run, not a ledger table of its own. Events already reach control signed, in order and once, through the relay's cursor; a full export keeps them with the run's other events; and control keeps them after a full reset, when a table in the wiped ledger would be gone. A migration adds an index on the ledger's events by kind, so the many records do not slow the reads of one kind. Control files each record as a row (`model_call`) at ingest, with its run's campaign, and the views it builds from every event leave the records out.
- 2026-10-21, build: a record covers what each program reports, never a guess. Pi: one call, its usage from pi-ai, with cached and reasoning tokens only when the provider's answer names them (pi-ai gives 0 otherwise), and the times from the request to the first and the last token. OpenCode 2.0.32: one step, its `TokenUsage.Info` (input without the cache, output without the reasoning, both added back), the first token from the step's first part, and the step's time only for a step that ran no tool (OpenCode ends a step after its tools). Codex 0.162.1: one turn, what it added to the thread's totals, with no count of calls and no times. Claude Code 2.1.305: one `claude -p` run, from its result (`usage`, `duration_api_ms`, `ttft_ms` less `time_to_request_ms`), with the calls its stream showed; a run cut off before its result keeps its stream's tokens, with no times. Output tokens a second is a record's output over its time in calls.
- 2026-10-21, build: a record names its agent by the internal identifiers (`workers`, `planner`, `teachers`, `combiner` for the teachers' merged by model, `auditor`, `panel` for the review panel), in one list with goal 074's words for them in `src/core/usage.ts`.
- 2026-10-21, build, on cost: control costs each record when it is read, at its model's price then, so a price the owner sets later costs the earlier calls too. The price comes from the provider's model list when the list has a `pricing` object (US dollars per token, as text: `prompt`, `completion`, `input_cache_read`), as OpenRouter's and Nous Portal's do (read from their documentation and Nous Portal's live list, 2026-10-21); OpenAI's own list, Anthropic's (its List Models fields) and OpenCode Zen's (its live list: `id`, `object`, `created`, `owned_by`) give none. A list's pricing `overrides` and its separate cache-write and reasoning prices are not used: cache-written input is priced as input, reasoning as output. Else the owner's price, kept on control (`POST /v1/model-prices`, MCP's `set_model_price`). A Claude or ChatGPT provider's calls, and every Claude Code call, are "on a plan"; any other call with no price is "no price", never 0. A RunPod pod's spend: each 30-second count control already makes goes to the run its rig was running then (split evenly between two; to no run, so only to the system, when none), recorded as a row, so a run's, a campaign's and a period's spend are sums of rows.
- 2026-10-21, build, on the screens (as the owner approved the mockup `v010-usage`, with its open choices as shown and as the cost step built them):
  - **Where.** A run's **Model use** is above its tabs, so it shows on every tab. A campaign's is in its page's sidebar: the campaign's page now has two columns, with At work now, the decisions, Earlier runs, Agents' context and Knowledge in the main one (Knowledge's own two columns stack there). **Metrics** is in the main navigation after Rigs, at `/ui/metrics`, with **7 days** as its default period. A run with no agents (a try of a kit) and nothing spent shows no block; a run with agents and no record yet says so.
  - **Today where the viewer is.** `GET /v1/usage` and `model_usage` take `tz`, an IANA time zone name (default `UTC`), and today starts at midnight there; the report says its `tz`. An unknown name is refused in words. The 7 days stay the last 7 times 24 hours. The dashboard's own script adds the browser's zone to every link to Metrics, and loads Metrics again with it when it is missing; without the script, Metrics counts from midnight UTC, and the line under its title always names the zone it uses.
  - **What the API gives for the screens.** The report adds `by_agent_model` (each agent's calls to each model: the run table's rows), and each cost adds `free` (records priced at 0), the tokens `on_plan_tokens`, `no_price_tokens` and `free_tokens`, and `priced_as_not_cached` (tokens in priced at the input price because their records do not report the cache, where the model's cached price is lower). So REST and MCP give every number the screens show, the words included.
  - **Words.** "not reported", "on a plan", "no price" and "free" as the mockup has them, and an amount under half a cent is "<$0.01", never $0.00. A free model is one whose listed price is 0 in every part.
  - **Teacher 1 and teacher 2.** Records name the teachers as one agent. When a run's teachers' records name two models, each line says "teacher 1" or "teacher 2" where the record's provider and model match exactly one of the two in the rig's settings now; else the line has no second word. The merged by model's line says "merged by".
  - **The bars under Calls.** A run's: its calls in each round, each record in the round that had started when it was made (the rounds' `epoch_started` events); none for a run with fewer than two rounds. Metrics': each hour of today, each day for 7 days and all, each week past 62 days, in the page's zone. A record that does not say how many calls it covers (a Codex turn) counts as one call in the bars only; the Calls number counts it as none, and its i says how many there are.
  - **"28 a trial".** The workers' calls over the trials their records name.
  - **GPU time on RunPod.** A run's row says its time as the pod's spend for the run over the pod's price an hour now (`5 h 36 m at $1.65/h`); without a known price, the rig alone. On Metrics, the row is the pods' whole spend in the period, also while no run was at work, as the cost step built it: that part is in no campaign.
  - **Metrics by model.** One row for each provider's model, with every harness that ran it, summed from its records (the API's `by_model` keeps each harness apart, as the mockup's rows do not).
  - **Prices in Settings › Providers.** Each provider with a model list gets **Prices, $ for a million tokens**: In, Cached in and Out for each model, its chip (`from the provider`, `free, from the provider`, `yours`, `no price`) and the line "So far: … · $…" that the page's script keeps up to date as the owner types (its part without the page is tested against the server's words). **Save prices** posts to `POST /ui/settings/providers/<provider>/prices`, which sets each changed price through the same function as `POST /v1/model-prices` (audited as `owner:ui`); all three fields empty removes the owner's price; a listed price can't be changed. A provider whose list gives only free models shows one line; a subscription says it is on a plan.
- 2026-10-21, owner, on the mockup `v010-usage` again: "[the By agent and model table] this should probably be in details under stats tab on a single run. You could probably collapse tokens out and tok/s into same card as tokens in. Number of calls can probly go into the stats tab on a single run. Time in calls card can probably just be a short text only clock at top <38 trials - 9 rounds - {total time} - {time in calls}>. Campaign looks fine enough, good start. Provider models price cards... way to much.. why is this nested inside a provider? What are we nesting dolls? Simplify simplify simplify. You can just have a simple table of model names below providers for custom pricing if needed, but for the love of all things holy don't ever do this super nested entire UI inside another UI inside another UI. Metrics page looks fine enough, good start." So (this replaces the run's six numbers and the prices in each provider above; the campaign's sidebar and Metrics stay as they are):
  - **A run's top.** One line, with an i: its trials, rounds, time and time in calls (`48 trials · 16 rounds · 30 h 0 m · 6 h 34 m in calls`). The run's time is from its start to now, or to its last event once it is closed; paused time counts. Then two cards: **Cost**, as before, and one card with **Tokens in** (and its split), **Tokens out** and **Output speed**. A run with no record yet ends the line with `no model call yet`, and has no cards.
  - **A Stats tab.** The run page had none, so it gets one, the last tab, after Planner (`?view=stats`), where the top shows (a run with agents, records or a pod's spend). On it: **Calls** (the count, "28 a trial", the median time to the first token, and a bar for each round with `round 1` and the latest round under them), then **By agent and model**, as before.
  - **Model prices.** The price fields inside each provider are gone. Under the Providers block, one plain table, **Model prices**: one row for each model of each provider that is not a subscription (Claude or ChatGPT), with Model, Provider, In, Cached in and Out ($ for a million tokens), and **Price from** (`provider's list`, `yours`, `free`, `no price`). A listed price is text, not a field. One **Save prices** posts every row to `POST /ui/settings/prices`, which replaces `POST /ui/settings/providers/<provider>/prices`; each change still goes through `setModelPrice`, audited as `owner:ui`. A refusal names the model and its provider (`small-model of lab: set In and Out, or leave all three empty.`), in the same words from the page's script (`Not yet.`) and from the server (`Not saved.`). The "So far" line under each model is gone, with the store's query for it.

## Open questions

None.

## Progress

- 2026-10-21: Goal written from the owner's words. Trials already record tokens in and out (`trial_finished`); cached tokens, the planner's and advisors' calls, and times are not recorded yet. A mockup comes first for the screens.
- 2026-10-21: Everything behind the screens is built. The workers (Pi through their own process and the trial's token; OpenCode, Codex and Claude Code from their output), the planner and the advisors record each call as a `model_call` event; the supervisor hands the advisors' to the harness (`POST /v1/model-calls`). Control sums them for a run, a campaign or the system, today, over 7 days or for all time: `GET /v1/usage` and the MCP tool `model_usage`. Tests cover each harness's records with and without cache figures, the sums and their percentiles, the periods, the not-reported case, REST and MCP. Pages: How the parts fit together (the records), the REST and MCP references, the advisors file and the glossary. Next: the screens, placed as the owner chose. The API's `today` starts at midnight UTC; the screens' "today" is in the viewer's time zone.
- 2026-10-21: Cost behind the screens is built: each sum's `cost` (its parts, a RunPod pod's spend, and the records priced, on a plan and with no price) in `GET /v1/usage` and `model_usage`; providers' listed prices kept with their model lists; the owner's prices with `GET`/`POST /v1/model-prices` and `set_model_price`, also listed by the `providers` tool. Tests: the list's prices, the cost sums, the plan and no-price cases, the pod spend's split, REST and MCP. Pages: the REST and MCP references, Connect a model provider, How the parts fit together, the glossary. Next: cost on the screens, with Settings › Providers' price field.
- 2026-10-21: The screens are built, as the owner approved the mockup `v010-usage`: a run's **Model use** at the top of its page (the six numbers, and a table by agent and model in The work, The advisors and, on RunPod, The rig), a campaign's in its page's sidebar (the totals and each run), a new **Metrics** page in the main navigation (today from midnight in the viewer's time zone, 7 days or all; by model and by campaign), and each model's price in **Settings › Providers**. `GET /v1/usage` and `model_usage` take `tz` and give `by_agent_model` and the cost's token figures. Tests: `src/control/usage-ui.test.ts` (each screen, the words, the teachers' lines, the RunPod row, today in a time zone over the page and REST, Save prices and its refusals, the price line's script against the server, the bars across a change of the clocks), `src/core/usage.test.ts` (today in a time zone, free and the token figures, by agent and model) and `src/control/usage.test.ts`. The dashboard demo (`scripts/dashboard-demo.ts`) has made-up model calls and a priced provider. Pages: a new reference page, Model use and cost; How the parts fit together (the dashboard's pages, the records), Connect a model provider (the price field), the REST and MCP references and the glossary. Every box is ticked. The control acceptance runs at roll time.
- 2026-10-21: The owner's second look is built, after the mockup `v010-usage` was revised for it (the owner's approval comes before the merge): a run's top is one line and two cards, its new **Stats** tab has the calls and **By agent and model**, and Settings › Providers has one **Model prices** table under the providers, with one Save (`POST /ui/settings/prices`). Tests: `src/control/usage-ui.test.ts` (the line, its time and its i, the two cards, the Stats tab and its bars, the run with no record and the try with no tab, the table with no subscription in it, Save and its refusals, the page's script against the server's words). Pages: Model use and cost, Connect a model provider, How the parts fit together, the glossary, Start a campaign from the dashboard, Hand the work to agents, and the changelog. Every box still holds.

